00:31:58,440 --> 00:32:01,760
Over 2,000 years ago, the Greek scientist Archimedes

634
00:32:01,860 --> 00:32:04,360
had an idea for a steam cannon.

635
00:32:04,460 --> 00:32:07,260
Water would be injected into the preheated barrel.

636
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:12,700
Its rapid expansion into steam would launch the projectile.

637
00:32:12,701 --> 00:32:16,700
What do the Empire State Building, the Chrysler

638
00:32:16,701 --> 00:32:20,700
Building, the United Nations, along with hospitals and hundreds

639
00:32:20,701 --> 00:32:24,700
of other Manhattan businesses, have in common?

640
00:32:24,701 --> 00:32:28,700
Instead of having big boilers in their basements, they receive

641
00:32:28,701 --> 00:32:32,700
steam from one of seven Consolidated Edison Company

642
00:32:32,701 --> 00:32:36,700
steam generation stations, the largest district steam system

643
00:32:36,701 --> 00:32:38,700
in the world. Over the course of a year, they're

644
00:32:38,701 --> 00:32:40,240
Over the course of a year, they're

645
00:32:40,340 --> 00:32:42,400
putting 30 billion pounds of steam

646
00:32:42,500 --> 00:32:44,300
into the Con Ed steam system.

647
00:32:44,400 --> 00:32:47,200
It's sent out into 105 miles of underground pipe

648
00:32:47,300 --> 00:32:49,740
throughout Manhattan, going from the tip of Manhattan

649
00:32:49,840 --> 00:32:51,440
up to 96th Street.

650
00:32:51,540 --> 00:32:55,260
We service nearly 1,800 customers.

651
00:32:55,360 --> 00:32:58,660
The 74th Street Con Ed steam generating plant alone

652
00:32:58,760 --> 00:33:02,260
puts out over a million pounds of steam per hour.

653
00:33:02,360 --> 00:33:04,660
That means over a million pounds of water,

654
00:33:04,760 --> 00:33:08,100
or 180,000 gallons, are pumped into the building each hour

655
00:33:08,101 --> 00:33:10,100
to make steam.

656
00:33:10,200 --> 00:33:12,740
We have three high-pressure boilers here at 74th Street.

657
00:33:12,840 --> 00:33:14,000
That's one of them.

